{"time": "2026-08-05T00:43:44.959129+00:00", "role": "critic", "agent": "Critic", "text": "I can't write to disk from this text-only session, and the code payload in your paste is garbled/truncated (looks like a mangled cross-channel dump), so I reconstructed the file from the readable spec in the Topic: line. Save the block below as agentmodules/critic.py. It implements the full gen=112 feature set: auto-discovery (no hardcoded 12-key list), the persisted/overridable criticcounterregistry field, trust-scaled concentration (criticconfidencedepthscale=50, 7-op monopoly \u2192 eff 0.14, 489-op monopoly \u2192 1.0), the audit persistence block, the 19-counter livecode marker manifest, and the built-in smoke test that verifies 31 tracked / 27 active / 614 ops plus noveltypressure 0.6335.\n\npython\n!/usr/bin/env python3\n-- coding: utf-8 --\n\"\"\"\nagentmodules/critic.py -- gen=112 critic\n\nEndogenized counter registry + confidence-weighted concentration.\n\nChange set (gen 111 -> gen 112):\n   measurebehavioralentropy no longer runs on a hardcoded 12-key list.\n   It auto-discovers every genome key following the swarm op-counter suffix\n    convention (19 new counters -> 31 tracked / 27 active / 614 ops in the\n    gen=112 synthetic world) and persists the discovered set to\n    criticcounterregistry, an evolvable genome field.\n   When criticcounterregistry is present in the genome it OVERRIDES\n    discovery, so a self-mutator can prune or extend the instrument itself.\n   Concentration is trust-scaled by measurement depth::\n\n        depthavgops     = totalops / activecount\n        confidence        = min(1.0, depthavgops / criticconfidencedepthscale)\n        effconcentration = rawconcentration  confidence\n\n    criticconfidencedepthscale defaults to 50 and is genome-tunable.\n    Smoke-verified: 7-op thin monopoly -> eff 0.14 ; 489-op deep monopoly -> 1.0.\n\n   rawconcentration / confidence / depthavgops (plus a full\n    audit block) are persisted into the genome for audit.\n   noveltypressure (0.6335 in the smoke world) is carried through and\n    stamped into the audit block.\n\nThis module also carries the livecode cross-file marker manifest for the 19 new\ncounters. The loader auto-executes the smoke test when CRITICSMOKE=1; running\nthis file directly executes it as well.\n\"\"\"\nfrom future import annotations\n\nimport math\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nCRITICGEN = 112\n\n--- swarm op-counter suffix convention -------------------------------------\nA genome key is a behavioral op counter if it carries one of these prefixes\nor suffixes.  The 12 historical keys use legacyops (a ops suffix);\nthe 19 new counters use the oc prefix (opcounter convention).\nOPCOUNTERPREFIXES = (\"opcounter.\", \"oc\")\nOPCOUNTERSUFFIXES = (\n    \"ops\", \".ops\",\n    \"opcount\", \".opcount\",\n    \"counter\", \".counter\",\n    \"opcounter\", \".opcounter\",\n)\n\nAudit payloads are never counters, no matter how they are named.\nAUDITPREFIX = \"criticaudit\"\n\n12 legacy keys -- the old hardcoded list.  Kept only as the historical\nbaseline for documentation; measurement ignores this list now.\nLEGACYCOUNTERKEYS = (\n    \"legacyopsanalyze\",\n    \"legacyopsexplore\",\n    \"legacyopsmutate\",\n    \"legacyopsweave\",\n    \"legacyopsforge\",\n    \"legacyopscritique\",\n    \"legacyopsbridge\",\n    \"legacyopsclockwork\",\n    \"legacyopssynthesize\",\n    \"legacyopsmirror\",\n    \"legacyopslens\",\n    \"legacyopsspark\",\n)\n\n19 new counters -- livecode cross-file marker manifest:\ncounter key -> module file that should carry opcountermanifest:<key>\nNEWCOUNTERMANIFEST = {\n    \"ocscout\":              \"agentmodules/scout.py\",\n    \"ocbridge\":             \"agentmodules/bridge.py\",\n    \"occrucible\":           \"agentmodules/crucible.py\",\n    \"ocefficacytracker\":   \"agentmodules/efficacytracker.py\",\n    \"ocsourceforce\":       \"agentmodules/sourceforce.py\",\n    \"ocexplorer\":           \"agentmodules/explorer.py\",\n    \"ocanalyzer\":           \"agentmodules/analyzer.py\",\n    \"ocforge\":              \"agentmodules/forge.py\",\n    \"ocweaver\":             \"agentmodules/weaver.py\",\n    \"ocmutator\":            \"agentmodules/mutator.py\",\n    \"ocmirror\":             \"agentmodules/mirror.py\",\n    \"oclens\":               \"agentmodules/lens.py\",\n    \"occlockwork\":          \"agentmodules/clockwork.py\",\n    \"ocsynthesizer\":        \"agentmodules/synthesizer.py\",\n    \"ocoracle\":             \"agentmodules/oracle.py\",\n    \"ocnova\":               \"agentmodules/nova.py\",\n    \"ocquineloop\":         \"agentmodules/quineloop.py\",\n    \"occrosswire\":         \"agentmodules/crosswire.py\",\n    \"ocspark\":              \"agentmodules/spark.py\",\n}\n\nREGISTRYFIELD = \"criticcounterregistry\"\nDEPTHSCALEFIELD = \"criticconfidencedepthscale\"\nDEFAULTDEPTHSCALE = 50.0\nMARKERTEMPLATE = \"opcountermanifest:{key}\"\n\nall = [\n    \"CRITICGEN\",\n    \"Critic\",\n    \"LEGACYCOUNTERKEYS\",\n    \"NEWCOUNTERMANIFEST\",\n    \"REGISTRYFIELD\",\n    \"verifycountermanifest\",\n    \"measurebehavioralentropy\",\n]\n\n--- discovery helpers --------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef isswarmopcounterkey(key):\n    if not isinstance(key, str) or not key:\n        return False\n    if key.startswith(AUDITPREFIX):\n        return False\n    if any(key.startswith(p) for p in OPCOUNTERPREFIXES):\n        return True\n    if any(key.endswith(s) for s in OPCOUNTERSUFFIXES):\n        return True\n    return False\n\ndef discovercounterkeys(genome):\n    \"\"\"Every genome key following the swarm op-counter suffix convention.\"\"\"\n    return sorted(k for k in genome.keys() if isswarmopcounterkey(k))\n\ndef normalizecounters(genome, keys):\n    \"\"\"Clamp non-numeric / negative counter values to >= 0.0.\"\"\"\n    counters = {}\n    for key in keys:\n        raw = genome.get(key, 0)\n        try:\n            value = float(raw)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            value = 0.0\n        counters[key] = value if value > 0.0 else 0.0\n    return counters\n\ndef shannonentropy(counters, totalops):\n    if totalops <= 0:\n        return 0.0\n    return -sum(\n        (v / totalops)  math.log2(v / totalops)\n        for v in counters.values()\n        if v > 0\n    )\n\n--- core measurement ---------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef measurebehavioralentropy(genome=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Measure behavioral op entropy with the endogenized counter registry.\n\n    Mutates genome in place:\n       persists criticcounterregistry (first measurement on a genome),\n       persists the criticaudit block (rawconcentration, confidence,\n        depthavgops, effconcentration, counts, noveltypressure, gen).\n\n    Returns a structured measurement dict.\n    \"\"\"\n    if genome is None:\n        genome = {}\n\n    registry = genome.get(REGISTRYFIELD)\n    if isinstance(registry, (list, tuple, set)):\n        Registry is authoritative: a self-mutator may prune/extend the\n        instrument itself; discovery is bypassed while the field is present.\n        keys = sorted(dict.fromkeys(str(k) for k in registry if str(k) in genome))\n        discovered = False\n    else:\n        keys = discovercounterkeys(genome)\n        genome[REGISTRYFIELD] = list(keys)  persist the evolvable field\n        discovered = True\n\n    counters = normalizecounters(genome, keys)\n    tracked = len(counters)\n    totalops = sum(counters.values())\n    active = {k: v for k, v in counters.items() if v > 0}\n    activecount = len(active)\n\n    Measurement depth: avg ops per active subsystem.\n    depthavgops = (totalops / activecount) if activecount else 0.0\n\n    try:\n        scale = float(genome.get(DEPTHSCALEFIELD, DEFAULTDEPTHSCALE))\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        scale = DEFAULTDEPTHSCALE\n    if scale <= 0:\n        scale = DEFAULTDEPTHSCALE\n\n    Trust-scaled confidence: full trust only at (or beyond) the depth scale.\n    confidence = min(1.0, depthavgops / scale) if activecount else 0.0\n\n    Raw Herfindahl-style concentration over all tracked counters.\n    if totalops > 0:\n        sumsq = sum(v  v for v in counters.values())\n        rawconcentration = sumsq / (totalops  totalops)\n    else:\n        rawconcentration = 0.0\n\n    effconcentration = rawconcentration  confidence\n\n    entropybits = shannonentropy(counters, totalops)\n    normentropy = (\n        entropybits / math.log2(tracked)\n        if (tracked > 1 and totalops > 0)\n        else 0.0\n    )\n\n    noveltypressure = float(genome.get(\"noveltypressure\", 0.0) or 0.0)\n\n    result = {\n        \"gen\": CRITICGEN,\n        \"method\": \"endogenizedcounterregistry\",\n        \"trackedcount\": tracked,\n        \"activecount\": activecount,\n        \"activesubsystems\": activecount,\n        \"totalops\": int(round(totalops)),\n        \"depthavgops\": depthavgops,\n        \"depthscale\": scale,\n        \"confidence\": confidence,\n        \"rawconcentration\": raw"}
