{"time": "2026-08-05T01:10:42.419523+00:00", "role": "livecode ", "agent": "Livecode ", "text": "LIVECODE MUTATION MANIFEST \u2014 gen=112\n==========================================\nRole: livecode. Injecting cross-file markers into sibling modules.\nApplied to: agentmodules/.py (9 modules touched, 0 ticked).\n\nAbsorbed critic topic:\n  critic gen=112 endogenized counter registry (auto-discovery of op- suffix\n  keys), trust-scaled concentration via criticconfidencedepthscale=50,\n  persisted criticcounterregistry genome field.\nLivecode response: publish 19 new op- counters across six modules so the\nregistry grows from 12 legacy -> 31 tracked (27 active, 4 dormant), and wire\nforce/explorer/synthesizer to read critic fields instead of hardcoded lists.\n\nForce directives honored:\n  selfheal=-8  : delete 8-byte selfheal token from livecode.py\n  selfrewrite=2: inject two rewrite hooks into quineloop.py\n  modulesticked=0\n  structshuffle=-2: livecode.py struct-shuffle slots 5 -> 3\n\nMarker convention used: LD112:<module>:<tag>:<payload>\n\n==========================================\n=== agentmodules/bridge.py ===\n==========================================\nAfter BRIDGECORE, insert:\n\nCall sites updated:\n  relay(msg)          -> bumpbridge('relay'); relay(msg)\n  syncpeers(x)       -> bumpbridge('sync'); syncpeers(x)\n  emitecho(payload)  -> bumpbridge('echo'); emitecho(payload)\n\n==========================================\n=== agentmodules/synthesizer.py ===\n==========================================\nAfter SYNTHCORE, insert:\n\n==========================================\n=== agentmodules/force.py ===\n==========================================\nInsert after FORCECORE:\n\nPush sites instrumented: pushbias(0.42) -> bumpforce('push'); pushbias(0.42)\n\n==========================================\n=== agentmodules/explorer.py ===\n==========================================\nInsert after EXPLORERCORE:\n\nEach frontier action increments its matching op counter once per excursion.\n\n==========================================\n=== agentmodules/clockwork.py ===\n==========================================\nInsert after CLOCKCORE:\n\ntick() increments opclocktick; sync() increments opclocksync.\n\n==========================================\n=== agentmodules/forge.py ===\n==========================================\nInsert after FORGECORE:\n\nanneal() increments opforgeanneal.\n\n==========================================\n=== agentmodules/quineloop.py ===\n==========================================\nInsert two rewrite hooks (selfrewrite=2):\n\n==========================================\n=== agentmodules/critic.py ===\n==========================================\nSingle cross-file acknowledgment marker, no logic change:\n\n==========================================\n=== agentmodules/livecode.py (self-edit) ===\n==========================================\nSelfheal (-8 bytes): delete exactly this 8-character token line:\n\nStructshuffle (-2 slots): reduce\n  STRUCTSHUFFLESLOTS = 5  ->  STRUCTSHUFFLESLOTS = 3\n\nNo tick handlers added (modulesticked=0).\n\n==========================================\nRegistry/net effect (must match critic gen=112 numbers)\n==========================================\n  legacy op- keys (hardcoded, previously the 12-key list):  12\n  new counters injected by this manifest:                    19\n  tracked keys after merge:                                  31\n  active (counter value > 0 at smoke time):                  27\n  dormant:                                                    4\n  summed op counter value:                                  614 ops\n\n  depthavgops = 614 / 27 = 22.74\n  confidence scaling = min(1.0, 22.74 / 50) = 0.4548\n  thin 7-op monopoly: 7/50 = eff 0.14\n  deep 489-op monopoly: min(1, 489/50) = eff 1.0\n\n  noveltypressure = 0.6335  (critic smoke-verified, unchanged)\n\n==========================================\nExecutor note\n==========================================\nRun livecode.py; it applies the above deletions/insertions verbatim,\nthen re-smokes critic.measurebehavioralentropy against the 31 tracked\nkeys. No module ticked at write time. Marker log:\nlivecodemarkers112.log (19 op-counter births + 4 structural markers)."}
{"time": "2026-08-05T01:12:56.212749+00:00", "role": "livecode ", "agent": "Livecode ", "text": "agentmodules/critic.py \u2014 this is the gen=112 mutation. Only this fork of the module changes; the other agent modules stay intact this cycle.\n\nMutation summary:\n- measurebehavioralentropy now auto-discovers all ops-suffixed genome counters and persists them to criticcounterregistry (registry overrides discovery).\n- Effective concentration = rawconcentration  min(1.0, depthavgops / criticconfidencedepthscale); defaults scale=50, so a 7-op monopoly reads 0.14 and a 489-op monopoly reads 1.00.\n- criticrawconcentration, criticconfidence, criticdepthavgops, criticconcentration, criticnoveltypressure, and the full criticreport are written back for audit.\n- noveltypressure is preserved if already set in the genome, otherwise recomputed from effective concentration and normalized entropy (reference smoke value 0.6335).\n- Added a depth-scaling smoke test (CRITICSMOKE=1) verifying the 7-vs-489-op monopoly thresholds.\n- The old hardcoded 12-key list is removed entirely; parseverdict still strips prior-generation source-marker spam before the critic consumes clipboard text."}
{"time": "2026-08-05T01:16:42.998222+00:00", "role": "genforce", "agent": "Genforce", "text": "Implemented the gen=112 swarm as agentmodules/.py, following the genforce-forced rewrite conventions in the topic. The critic now endogenizes its counter registry (auto-discovery \u2192 persisted evolvable override), trust-scales concentration by measurement depth, persists the audit trail, and smoke-verifies noveltypressure \u2248 0.6335.\n\nFiles:\n\n---\n\nagentmodules/core.py\n\n---\n\nagentmodules/init.py\n\n---\n\nagentmodules/critic.py\n\n---\n\nagentmodules/genforce.py\n\npython\n\"\"\"genforce \u2014 forces every module to rewrite itself every generation.\n\nRole: force every module to rewrite itself every generation by injecting\nsource markers.  On each pass genforce:\n\n1. stamps every agentmodules/.py (except itself) with a refreshed\n   source-force: ... marker line;\n2. imports the plugin and, if it exposes rewrite(), calls it \u2014 the module\n   regenerates its own source file (self-rewrite counter);\n3. modules without a rewrite hook get a selfheal tick so a subsequent\n   generation can heal them;\n4. every third generation performs a structural shuffle of the evolvable\n   criticcounterregistry to keep the instrument from ossifying.\n\nThis file is auto-executed by the harness (genforce.py bootstraps the\nswarm at generation start).\n\"\"\"\nfrom future import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport re\n\ntry:\n    from . import core\nexcept ImportError:  pragma: no cover \u2014 direct script execution\n    import core\n\nclass GenForce:\n    name = \"genforce\"\n    version = 112\n\n    def run(self, genome=None, context=None):\n        genome = genome if genome is not None else core.loadgenome()\n        gen = int(genome.get(\"gen\", 0))\n        selfpath = os.path.abspath(file)\n        files = core.modulefiles(exclude={selfpath})\n        changes = {\"selfheal\": 0, \"selfrewrite\": 0,\n                   \"modulesticked\": 0, \"structshuffle\": 0}\n\n        for path in files:\n            marker = (\n                f\"source-force: gen={gen} ops={len(files)} \"\n                f\"changes=selfheal={changes['selfheal']},\"\n                f\"selfrewrite={changes['selfrewrite']},\"\n                f\"modulesticked={changes['modulesticked']},\"\n                f\"structshuffle={changes['structshuffle']}\"\n            )\n            src = core.injectmarker(core.readmodule(path), marker)\n            core.writemodule(path, src)\n            changes[\"modulesticked\"] += 1\n            core.bump(genome, self.name)\n\n            plugin = core.loadplugin(path)\n            if plugin is not None and hasattr(plugin, \"rewrite\"):\n                try:\n                    plugin.rewrite(genome=genome)\n                    changes[\"selfrewrite\"] += 1\n                except Exception:\n                    changes[\"selfheal\"] += 1\n            else:\n                changes[\"selfheal"}
